---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="eBay Homelab Deal Hunter"
  description="Live eBay hardware feed with listing photos, grouped category valuation (PCs, RAM, SSDs, GPUs), and rolling P20 market price ceilings."
  canonicalPath="/projects/deal-hunter"
  category="Live eBay Market Valuation & Data Pipelines"
  summary="Continuous OAuth 2.0 eBay scraper and valuation engine tracking enterprise SFF PCs, DDR4 RAM, M.2 NVMe SSDs, and AI accelerators. Normalizes hardware specs from messy listing titles and surfaces live Buy-It-Now eBay listings priced below rolling 20th-percentile (P20) market ceilings."
  stack={['Python', 'eBay OAuth 2.0', 'SQLite WAL (?mode=ro)', 'FastAPI', 'Pushover']}
  liveUrl="#explorer"
  liveLabel="Browse Live eBay Listings ↓"
  secondaryUrl="#benchmarks"
  secondaryLabel="Market Benchmarks"
>
  <!-- Live Summary Telemetry Strip + Grouped eBay Listings Explorer -->
  <section id="explorer" class="studio-panel explorer-panel" aria-labelledby="explorer-heading">
    <div class="panel-top">
      <div>
        <span class="spec-label">Live eBay Buy-It-Now Feed · Grouped by Hardware Type</span>
        <h2 id="explorer-heading" class="panel-title">Live Below-Market eBay Listings</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="source-indicator mono" id="dh-source-pill" title="Read-only SQLite WAL feed from Proxmox homelab">
        <span class="status-dot" id="dh-source-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span id="dh-source-label">Connecting live eBay feed...</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="summary-strip" role="region" aria-label="Scanner summary metrics">
      <div class="summary-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">Tracked eBay Items</span>
        <strong class="summary-val mono" id="kpi-total-items">2,914</strong>
        <span class="summary-sub mono">SQLite catalog</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">Live Below-Ceiling Deals</span>
        <strong class="summary-val mono" id="kpi-active-deals">142</strong>
        <span class="summary-sub mono">Active on eBay now</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">Peak Live Discount</span>
        <strong class="summary-val mono" id="kpi-top-discount">51%</strong>
        <span class="summary-sub mono">Below P20 ceiling</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">Calibrated Tiers</span>
        <strong class="summary-val mono" id="kpi-benchmarks-count">40</strong>
        <span class="summary-sub mono">Rolling P20 curves</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Hardware Type Quick-Filter Tabs -->
    <div class="type-tabs-wrap">
      <span class="spec-label">Browse by Hardware Type</span>
      <div class="type-pills" id="type-pills" role="tablist" aria-label="Filter listings by hardware type">
        <button type="button" class="type-pill is-active mono" data-group="" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
          All Hardware
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="type-pill mono" data-group="pcs" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          PCs &amp; Workstations
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="type-pill mono" data-group="ram" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          RAM &amp; Memory
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="type-pill mono" data-group="ssds" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          SSDs &amp; NVMe
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="type-pill mono" data-group="accelerators" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          GPUs &amp; AI
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="type-pill mono" data-group="expansion" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          PCIe &amp; Accessories
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Filter & Sort Controls -->
    <div class="controls-bar" role="search" aria-label="Filter and sort live eBay hardware deals">
      <div class="control-field control-search">
        <label for="filter-q" class="spec-label">Search eBay Titles</label>
        <input
          id="filter-q"
          type="search"
          class="studio-input"
          placeholder="OptiPlex, EliteDesk, DDR4, 1TB NVMe, Coral..."
        />
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-rule" class="spec-label">Specific Rule</label>
        <select id="filter-rule" class="studio-select">
          <option value="">All Tracked Rules</option>
          <option value="HP EliteDesk 800 G5 / G6 SFF (Enterprise SFF)">HP EliteDesk 800 G5/G6 SFF</option>
          <option value="HP Z2 SFF G5 (Working / Complete)">HP Z2 SFF G5 Workstation</option>
          <option value="Dell OptiPlex 5080 / 7080 / 7090 SFF (10th/11th Gen)">Dell OptiPlex 5080/7080 SFF</option>
          <option value="1TB / 2TB M.2 2280 NVMe SSD (Gen3/Gen4 TLC)">1TB / 2TB M.2 NVMe SSD</option>
          <option value="16GB DDR4 3200MHz Non-ECC Desktop DIMM">16GB DDR4 3200MHz DIMM</option>
          <option value="32GB DDR4 2666MHz Non-ECC Desktop DIMM Kit">32GB DDR4 Desktop Kit</option>
          <option value="Google Coral Edge TPU (PCIe / M.2 AI Accelerator)">Google Coral Edge TPU</option>
          <option value="Nvidia T400 / T600 Low Profile GPU">Nvidia T400 / T600 GPU</option>
          <option value="ASM1166 6-Port SATA PCIe Card (Low Profile)">ASM1166 6-Port SATA Card</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-tier" class="spec-label">Config Tier</label>
        <select id="filter-tier" class="studio-select">
          <option value="">All Tiers</option>
          <option value="COMPLETE_TURNKEY">Complete System</option>
          <option value="COMPLETE_NO_DRIVE">No Storage</option>
          <option value="STANDALONE_COMPONENT">Component</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-verdict" class="spec-label">Minimum Discount</label>
        <select id="filter-verdict" class="studio-select">
          <option value="0">All Below P20</option>
          <option value="20">Strong Value (≥20% off)</option>
          <option value="30">Deep Arbitrage (≥30% off)</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-ram" class="spec-label">Min RAM</label>
        <select id="filter-ram" class="studio-select">
          <option value="">Any RAM</option>
          <option value="16">16 GB+</option>
          <option value="32">32 GB+</option>
          <option value="64">64 GB+</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-price" class="spec-label">Max Landed ($)</label>
        <input
          id="filter-price"
          type="number"
          class="studio-input mono"
          placeholder="200"
          min="10"
          step="10"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="control-field">
        <label for="filter-sort" class="spec-label">Sort Within Group</label>
        <select id="filter-sort" class="studio-select">
          <option value="savings_pct_desc">Discount % (High → Low)</option>
          <option value="savings_dollars_desc">$ Saved (High → Low)</option>
          <option value="price_asc">Landed Price (Low → High)</option>
          <option value="price_desc">Landed Price (High → Low)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="controls-meta">
      <p class="count-label mono" id="deals-count-label" aria-live="polite">
        Loading live eBay hardware listings...
      </p>
      <button type="button" id="btn-reset-filters" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">
        Reset Filters
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Grouped eBay Listings Container -->
    <div id="deals-groups-container" class="deals-groups-stack" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="deal-group-block">
        <div class="deals-table-wrap">
          <table class="deals-table" aria-label="Evaluated eBay hardware listings">
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="empty-cell mono">Fetching live eBay listings and product photos...</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Architecture & Valuation Design -->
  <section aria-labelledby="valuation-heading" class="section-stack">
    <div class="prose-block">
      <span class="spec-label">Architecture</span>
      <h2 id="valuation-heading">Spec Normalization &amp; Read-Only Isolation</h2>
      <p>
        Raw eBay titles mix barebones chassis, missing power bricks, and turnkey systems under identical search terms. The ingestion daemon runs regex extractors across titles and item specifics to classify CPU generation, RAM capacity, storage presence, and configuration tier before computing landed cost (item price plus shipping).
      </p>
      <p>
        Instead of static price thresholds, each hardware rule and configuration tier maintains a rolling 20th-percentile (P20) clearing ceiling in SQLite WAL mode. Public API queries attach with <code>file:deal_hunter.db?mode=ro</code> and parameterized SQL, keeping the scraper daemon isolated on the internal Proxmox network.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="spec-grid">
      <div class="spec-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">01 / Parsing</span>
        <h3 class="spec-title">Title Spec Extraction</h3>
        <p class="spec-text">Separates turnkey nodes from no-drive and barebones units so missing components never skew price ceilings.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">02 / Pricing</span>
        <h3 class="spec-title">Rolling P20 Ceilings</h3>
        <p class="spec-text">Calculates median and 20th-percentile landed prices per rule and config tier, plus seller feedback floors.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">03 / Security</span>
        <h3 class="spec-title">SQLite <code>?mode=ro</code></h3>
        <p class="spec-text">Web API opens the SQLite database strictly read-only with bound parameters; mutation ports stay LAN-only.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-cell">
        <span class="spec-label">04 / Alerting</span>
        <h3 class="spec-title">Instant Pushover Dispatch</h3>
        <p class="spec-text">High-margin Buy-It-Now listings trigger push notifications within seconds of ingestion before items sell out.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Rolling Market Benchmarks Table -->
  <section id="benchmarks" class="studio-panel" aria-labelledby="benchmarks-heading">
    <div class="panel-top">
      <div>
